<title>INDIA: India's Congress seeks no changes in budget - Singh.</title>
<headline>India's Congress seeks no changes in budget - Singh.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Congress party said on Tuesday that it will not seek any changes in the budget proposals for fiscal 1997/98 (April-March) presented by former finance minister P. Chidambaram.</p>
<p>&quot;Reports that we are seeking to change the budget are wrong and baseless,&quot; former finance minister Manmohan Singh, the Congress party's economic policy advisor, told Reuters. &quot;I see no problem in the passage of the budget.&quot;</p>
</text>
